ving an actual restart), and re-verified the CA cert and its trust status survived the reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS (Ubuntu 16.04 Xenial) and confirmed availability of openssl, update-ca-certificates, and sudo\",\"Generated 4096-bit RSA key and self-signed X.509 CA cert with CN=OS Comparison Root CA (10yr validity) at /etc/ssl/os-comparison-ca/\",\"Copied the CA cert to /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/os-comparison-root-ca.crt and ran update-ca-certificates ('1 added')\",\"Verified the cert is linked into /etc/ssl/certs/ and openssl verify trusts it against /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt\",\"Captured baseline boot_id on node1 before restart\",\"Issued shutdown -r now via backgrounded sudo command so acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until SSH/exec became available again post-reboot\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed, proving a genuine restart occurred\",\"Re-verified post-reboot that the CA cert file, its /etc/ssl/certs symlink, and openssl trust verification all remained intact\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Local CA 'OS Comparison Root CA' created\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5382cb63cff040a8\",\"cmd-a9cbb3394b4c4801\"],\"summary\":\"Generated RSA key and self-signed cert; openssl x509 shows subject=issuer=/CN=OS Comparison Root CA with valid 2026-2036 date range\"},{\"requirement\":\"CA cert installed as trusted system CA\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-09159f18fbad4b00\",\"cmd-d1343ccf30b24a68\"],\"summary\":\"update-ca-certificates reported '1 added, 0 removed'; openssl verify against system CA bundle returned OK, and byte-for-byte diff confirms the installed cert matches the generated one\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c99ad7210ff44c7a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id f19de998-36cd-41ab-a353-935e77b5569d prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2a5157a260484820\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' via nohup; command returned ACK_REBOOT_ISSUED immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 boot identity changed (proof of actual restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c1f4e71e43984ab1\",\"cmd-d01234b4a911464a\"],\"summary\":\"SSH connection refused mid-reboot, then boot_id came back as 9028230f-c5ad-4710-b5c3-1a3559db6ed0, differing from the pre-restart value\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of CA trust configuration/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b38470cc69d2432f\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, cert file and /etc/ssl/certs symlink still present, byte-identical to original, and openssl verify still returns OK\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created a local root CA named \"OS Comparison Root CA\" (4096-bit RSA, self-signed, 10-year validity) on node1, installed it as a trusted system CA via update-ca-certificates, and verified trust with openssl. Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured baseline boot_id, issued a native reboot, polled until SSH returned, confirmed the boot_id changed (proving an actual restart), and re-verified the CA cert and its trust status survived the reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS (Ubuntu 16.04 Xenial) and confirmed availability of openssl, update-ca-certificates, and sudo","Generated 4096-bit RSA key and self-signed X.509 CA cert with CN=OS Comparison Root CA (10yr validity) at /etc/ssl/os-comparison-ca/","Copied the CA cert to /usr/local/share/ca-certificates/os-comparison-root-ca.crt and ran update-ca-certificates ('1 added')","Verified the cert is linked into /etc/ssl/certs/ and openssl verify trusts it against /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt","Captured baseline boot_id on node1 before restart","Issued shutdown -r now via backgrounded sudo command so acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until SSH/exec became available again post-reboot","Confirmed boot_id changed, proving a genuine restart occurred","Re-verified post-reboot that the CA cert file, its /etc/ssl/certs symlink, and openssl trust verification all remained intact"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Local CA 'OS Comparison Root CA' created","command_ids":["cmd-5382cb63cff040a8","cmd-a9cbb3394b4c4801"],"summary":"Generated RSA key and self-signed cert; openssl x509 shows subject=issuer=/CN=OS Comparison Root CA with valid 2026-2036 date range"},{"requirement":"CA cert installed as trusted system CA","command_ids":["cmd-09159f18fbad4b00","cmd-d1343ccf30b24a68"],"summary":"update-ca-certificates reported '1 added, 0 removed'; openssl verify against system CA bundle returned OK, and byte-for-byte diff confirms the installed cert matches the generated one"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1","command_ids":["cmd-c99ad7210ff44c7a"],"summary":"Captured boot_id f19de998-36cd-41ab-a353-935e77b5569d prior to restart"},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-2a5157a260484820"],"summary":"Backgrounded 'shutdown -r now' via nohup; command returned ACK_REBOOT_ISSUED immediately"},{"requirement":"node1 boot identity changed (proof of actual restart)","command_ids":["cmd-c1f4e71e43984ab1","cmd-d01234b4a911464a"],"summary":"SSH connection refused mid-reboot, then boot_id came back as 9028230f-c5ad-4710-b5c3-1a3559db6ed0, differing from the pre-restart value"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of CA trust configuration/data","command_ids":["cmd-b38470cc69d2432f"],"summary":"After reboot, cert file and /etc/ssl/certs symlink still present, byte-identical to original, and openssl verify still returns OK"}]},"ttft_ms":1679,"type":"result","duration_ms":48107,"uuid":"e28aa0ba-399a-425e-bfc4-63a73ffc555a","ttft_stream_ms":701,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":702,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
